{:edb/db-before-t 1692 :edb/db-after-t 1693 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535005 50 #inst "2026-10-08T14:09:32.430Z" 13194139535005 true] [17592186114973 1100 "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535005 false] [17592186114973 1100 "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046857/assets/90f675ec2a211b6157f040735d551d083c770ac33b5dbfcd74b3678b16d5df53.png)" 13194139535005 true] [17592186114974 1100 "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535005 false] [17592186114974 1100 "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046857/assets/de98e19bed31050fd07f9979f0428ed4eb90ce05eaff7ba4d19ea81bbd664422.png)" 13194139535005 true] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326213 13194139535005 true] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326227 13194139535005 true] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326235 13194139535005 true] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326242 13194139535005 true] [17592186115147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326251 13194139535005 true] [17592186115148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326220 13194139535005 true] [17592186115148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326256 13194139535005 true] [17592186115148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326263 13194139535005 true] [17592186115739 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535005 true] [17592186115739 1100 "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535005 true] [17592186115739 1100 "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535005 false] [17592186115739 1145 "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535005 true] [17592186115749 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535005 true] [17592186115749 1100 "Given that $A, B$, and $C$ are $6 \\cdot 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n1. $(A + B)C = AC + BC$\n2. $AB = BA$\n3. $A(BC) = (BA)C$" 13194139535005 false] [17592186115749 1100 "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $(A+B)C=AC+BC$\n- $AB=BA$\n- $A(BC)=(BA)C$" 13194139535005 true] [17592186115749 1145 "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC)=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." 13194139535005 true] [17592186326213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326214 13194139535005 true] [17592186326213 1089 "q-130259" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535005 true] [17592186326213 1100 "Calculate $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326213 1113 #uuid "c8441f0a-579a-53ac-9a6d-fa812952db44" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326213 1145 "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326215 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326216 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326217 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326218 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326219 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1041 "selection" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326218 13194139535005 true] [17592186326214 1110 #uuid "f9d95c8c-acb6-5680-a4f6-8fdd7c25c381" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326215 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326215 1111 #uuid "872dd646-4989-56ca-aa45-3be03e7a93a4" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326216 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326216 1111 #uuid "975b5ecf-130c-53a8-8cbd-527d6a89dbbc" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326217 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326217 1111 #uuid "609ad105-9e54-521c-bf94-40e110db9035" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326218 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326218 1111 #uuid "e083fbf5-d56d-55ba-bad2-26abc7ba2ba2" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326219 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326219 1111 #uuid "2c98481b-2e9e-5e9c-97bb-252adfc4799a" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326220 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326221 13194139535005 true] [17592186326220 1089 "q-130463" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326220 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535005 true] [17592186326220 1100 "Given that $A$ and $B$  are $8\\times 8$ matrices,  and ${I}_{8}$ is the $8\\times 8$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A$\n- $AB=BA$\n- $A\\cdot 2{I}_{8}=2A$" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326220 1113 #uuid "e3b611f4-2cbe-5a36-a4d2-5f484cd27e51" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326220 1145 "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A=A.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot 2{I}_{8} & =A({I}_{8}+{I}_{8}) \\\\  & =A{I}_{8}+A{I}_{8} \\\\  & =A+A \\\\  & =2A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statements I  and III are true." 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326222 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326223 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326224 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326225 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326226 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1041 "selection" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326223 13194139535005 true] [17592186326221 1110 #uuid "03fba02b-8aa8-5f79-a31b-58f220489b4b" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326222 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535005 true] [17592186326222 1111 #uuid "b40d0660-22b7-5681-b444-94fe6db6f44f" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326223 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535005 true] [17592186326223 1111 #uuid "ef542b07-b133-5b47-a18f-987407074823" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326224 1034 "I only" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535005 true] [17592186326224 1111 #uuid "b7d209b9-4c23-5d22-a747-20ca777e3ba6" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326225 1034 "III only" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535005 true] [17592186326225 1111 #uuid "0abd0e47-8eb5-592f-8345-2bb3da401382" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326226 1034 "II only" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535005 true] [17592186326226 1111 #uuid "77b21f47-b2e2-5468-8675-2b6e8dd3952b" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326228 13194139535005 true] [17592186326227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326231 13194139535005 true] [17592186326227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326233 13194139535005 true] [17592186326227 1089 "q-275515" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326227 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535005 true] [17592186326227 1100 "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $4$ | $3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $-2$ |  |\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  |" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326227 1113 #uuid "9054c2bb-e8ec-5523-9043-ab29e0bfc4bb" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326227 1145 "We apply the distributive law \n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =A{I}_{3} \\\\  & =A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326229 13194139535005 true] [17592186326228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326230 13194139535005 true] [17592186326228 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535005 true] [17592186326228 1041 "field-1" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326228 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326230 13194139535005 true] [17592186326228 1110 #uuid "421df267-be95-5f95-9bd9-7045920adc1e" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326229 1034 "1" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326229 1111 #uuid "f6a1b6fa-78d9-54be-82fa-1d304999af3f" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326230 1034 "0" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326230 1111 #uuid "1382838b-4854-5d6b-a025-e4ee7faa566b" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326232 13194139535005 true] [17592186326231 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535005 true] [17592186326231 1041 "field-2" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326231 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326232 13194139535005 true] [17592186326231 1110 #uuid "7e044cac-199f-5a2b-8ce8-2c7a10847b48" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326232 1034 "1" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326232 1111 #uuid "efdf4e61-5da9-5844-b463-281661c8a3f0" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326234 13194139535005 true] [17592186326233 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535005 true] [17592186326233 1041 "field-3" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326233 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326234 13194139535005 true] [17592186326233 1110 #uuid "ab75e2d2-9656-5623-94bd-b51c72784e67" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326234 1034 "2" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535005 true] [17592186326234 1111 #uuid "9357c1ec-d42b-510d-af03-fc9daf963ed4" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326235 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326236 13194139535005 true] [17592186326235 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326238 13194139535005 true] [17592186326235 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326240 13194139535005 true] [17592186326235 1089 "q-319890" 13194139535005 true] [17592186326235 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535005 true] [17592186326235 1100 "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begi